   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1: UNDP Country Offices and partners will have increased capability for scanning, sensemaking and experimentation for sustainable development solutions in 60 developing countries.

1.1	Number of new data sources used at Country Office level.
1.2	Number of diverse types data sources used
1.3	Number of sustainable development solutions identified and documented  
1.4	Number of innovation methods used to test and iterate over the different hypotheses.

Output 2: New sustainable development solutions will be scaled at country level as part of UNDP&#x2019;s country programme and operations, national policy and/or local markets. 

2.1 Number of publications ?? communication stories the Accelerator Lab Network shares with a public audience (outside of UNDP)
2.2 Percentage of lab insights, processes or products which are taken up by governments or other partners
2.3 Number partners and governments that increase their take up of the innovation methods included in the Accelerator Lab Network suite
2.4 Proportion of UNDP Country Office programming influenced by the Accelerator Lab Network&#x2019;s work and methodologies

Output 3: A core global level result will be that a global learning and scaling network is established and functioning.

3.1 Number of network interactions among the Accelerator Labs
3.2 Proportion of new models, approaches, and insights documented and disseminated throughout the network.
3.3 Number of engagements of the broader development ecosystem with published learnings from the Accelerator Lab Network.
3.4 Number of engagements on social media related to learnings and methods of the Accelerator Lab Networks with the broader development ecosystem</narrative>
    </description>
